## ✅ BellevueWeather Flow — Built & Validated

**File:** `BellevueWeather/BellevueWeather/BellevueWeather.flow`

### What was built

A 6-node linear flow that checks current weather for **Bellevue, WA** and tells you if it's a nice day:

| Node | Type | What it does |
|---|---|---|
| **Manual trigger** | `core.trigger.manual` | Starts the flow on demand |
| **Fetch Weather** | `core.action.http.v2` | GET request to the free [Open-Meteo API](https://open-meteo.com) — no API key needed. Fetches current temperature (°F), wind speed (mph), and weather code for Bellevue, WA (47.61°N, 122.20°W) |
| **Assess Weather** | `core.action.script` | JS script that evaluates: temp 60–85°F + weather code 0–3 (clear/partly cloudy) + wind < 20 mph → `isNiceDay: true/false` + a human-readable `message` |
| **Is it a nice day?** | `core.logic.decision` | Branches on `assessWeather1.output.isNiceDay === true` |
| **Nice Day - End** | `core.control.end` | Reached when it's nice out |
| **Not Nice - End** | `core.control.end` | Reached when conditions aren't ideal |

### Status
- ✅ **Validation:** Passed (`Status: Valid`)
- ✅ **Format:** Run (6 nodes repositioned, 2 resized)
- ✅ **No mock placeholders** — uses the real Open-Meteo public API
- ✅ **No connections required** — manual HTTP mode, no auth needed

